# Normalize line endings: the repo is developed on Windows but runs on Colab (Linux).
# Text files are stored with LF in the repo and checked out with the platform's native EOL.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Windows-only helper scripts keep CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
# Treat notebooks as text so diffs work, but don't let editors reformat them.
*.ipynb text eol=lf
# --- Git LFS -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The pretrained encoders (~294 MB across 10 files) are committed so that a clone of this
# repository is self-contained: code + notebooks + weights, no external release to fetch.
# They are stored in LFS rather than as plain blobs to keep the git history usable.
#
# NOTE for anyone cloning: you need git-lfs installed, otherwise the .pt files arrive as
# ~130-byte pointer text files and torch.load will fail. See README.md ("Cloning").
*.pt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Binary assets -- never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.pth binary
*.npz binary
*.npy binary
